  "preparedOwnedCoverage": [
    "Real controlled package signs/uploads, deliberately loses Upgrade response; real late Vault lease rejects actual modern-profile expiry while still-valid 30-day owned TLS cert permits only fresh Lookup",
    "Real revoked/unpublished signing material plus real interrupted AFC upload: owned authenticated cleanup returns ready but cannot retire/reprepare/resubmit",
    "Actual AppOwner bootstrap -> record-only context -> actual Keychain persistent identity resolution/import -> explicit existing Lookup; signing error remains after recovery",
    "Ready record cannot grant recovery; wrong device pin and deterministic pre-admission cancellation leave actual journal bytes unchanged and do not consume another network request",
    "Actual scoped Keychain missing/invalid UTF8/size/migration failure; old legacy load still returns readable value after rejected protection migration",
    "Actual owned Vault manifest UTF8 corruption preserves typed failure; explicit error-value assertions separately lock conservative no-storage/no-cancel fallback policy"
  ],
  "remaining": [
    "All 6 new methods are definitions only. Windows grammar is not Swift typecheck, SDK, Keychain, TLS or App acceptance",
    "No new private key enrolment/CSR, developer certificate/profile issuance or pairing authorization/import lifecycle; configuration only references an already existing accessible identity",
    "No signing-preparation/install button, new scheduler, automatic submission or completed-install next renewal cycle is implemented here",
    "Inaccessible/corrupt journal or Keychain read errors deliberately fail rather than select recovery-only. No endpoint or identity is invented",
    "Current Bundle material failure must be a known classified semantic/crypto failure; unknown/read-race/budget/storage failures retain their actual type and no fallback",
    "Lookup and cleanup do not establish Apple authority, installation success/renewed profile, physical same-device/no-VPN permission, kernel-loaded image, cold launch or all user-data preservation",
